    "diagnosis": "Corticotroph PitNET",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Loss of nuclear p27 reactivity is a frequent finding in corticotroph PitNETs. This finding is more frequent in functioning corticotroph tumours than in silent corticotroph tumours. This photomicrograph illustrates p27 loss in a functioning densely granulated corticotroph tumour. Note the preserved nuclear p27 expression in the non-tumorous elements (endothelial cells).",
